It was to activate the showscore option on that server so that the recent
problem with eit_brad's game evaporating and us having to reconstruct the score
wouldn't happen again.

There are _many_ compile-time options you can change in NetHack without braking
saved game file compatibility and the "official" statement on which ones are
which is that any option which doesn't affect saved game file formats can be
safely changed.  Since the showscore option has nothing to do with game play or
saved games in any way, there's no reason for it to have any affect on
compatibility (in fact, if it did that would be quite a serious bug).

As I said, however, the first instances of this actually happened _before_ I
swapped the binaries (before, in fact, I had even started the compile since the
rash of disappearing games was the _reason_ we needed to activate the showscore
option in the first place).

